-- title:
--   Integrality of a base change of the two-chart integral model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a non-zero element. For a subset $S \subseteq F$ write $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,S$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $\,R[S]$ generated by $S$; thus $A_{\mathrm{fin}} = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}$, $A_{\mathrm{inf}} = \mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ and $A_{\mathrm{mid}} = \mathrm{chartAlgMid}$ are the integral closures in $F$ of $R[j]$, $R[j^{-1}]$ and $R[j, j^{-1}]$ respectively. The scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout in schemes of the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{mid}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{mid}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ induced by the inclusions, and `toBase R F j` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ obtained from the two structure maps $R \to A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $R \to A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ by the universal property of the pushout. Let $k$ be a commutative $R$-algebra and assume that $k \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $k \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ are integral domains and that $k \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{mid}}$ is non-zero. Then the fibre product of `toBase R F j` with $\operatorname{Spec}(k) \to \operatorname{Spec}(R)$ is an integral scheme, that is, irreducible and reduced.
--
--   The two-chart integral model glues the integral closures of $R[j]$ and $R[j^{-1}]$ in $F$ along their overlap, and this statement gives a purely ring-theoretic criterion for a base change of it along $R \to k$ to remain integral. It is used in the construction and analysis of integral models of modular curves, for instance in establishing geometric integrality of base changes and irreducibility of models of $X_1(p)$ and of Hecke-type level structures.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isIntegral_pullback_toBase_of_isDomain_tensorProduct_chartAlg.lean

